WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.767
-Welcome back to the show,
Elvis Costello.

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:03.901
You know how to do it.
Welcome back.

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:05.501
-We're having quite a night
already.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:06.934
-We already have, right?

00:00:06.934 --> 00:00:08.501
-I've been on stage all week,

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:09.868
and I haven't heard my name
so much.

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.267
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]
How about that?

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:13.133
Madonna learned how to
play drums.

00:00:13.133 --> 00:00:14.901
-I know, isn't that fantastic?
-Did you ever hear that?

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.267
-Pete Thomas is backstage,
and he said,

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:19.601
he's promised free lessons.

00:00:19.601 --> 00:00:21.634
-Wow, there you go.

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:23.434
-And then we can have
the stand-off here.

00:00:23.434 --> 00:00:25.734
I think we need to do
"Into the Groove"

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:26.834
and "Pump It Up."

00:00:26.834 --> 00:00:27.901
I think that's what, yeah.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:29.634
[ Cheering ]

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:31.968
-"Into the Groove,"
is that your Madonna...

00:00:31.968 --> 00:00:34.534
-That's the one.
That's the one for me.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.801
I mean,
there's so many good ones.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:38.901
I mean, 50 number 1s?
-That's insane.

00:00:38.901 --> 00:00:41.667
-I mean, I've got 600 songs
in my catalogue,

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:42.934
and none of them were number 1s.

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:44.267
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.601
That's another record
in itself.

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:46.901
-Yeah, it's a record
in itself there, yeah.

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.267
-It really is.

00:00:48.267 --> 00:00:50.634
But have you guys
ever hung out, you and Madonna?

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.200
-You know, we did, and here's --

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.767
Can I tell this?

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:56.701
-She's probably in her limousine
at this point, yeah.

00:00:56.701 --> 00:01:00.300
-No, actually, her
brother-in-law, Joe Henry,

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.067
produced the record
"The River in Reverse,"

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:04.400
that I made with
Allen Toussaint,

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.434
a record very close to my heart.

00:01:06.434 --> 00:01:09.267
And he said one evening,
he said,

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:11.300
"We're gonna do a show at
the Village Vanguard.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:13.267
Do you want to come
to the show?"

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.767
And we went to
the Village Vanguard,

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:17.000
which is really close to
where we live here in New York,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.868
and the table was set up
for Joe, his sister-in-law,

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:22.200
my wife Diana, and myself.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.868
And we sat in the middle of
the Village Vanguard

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:27.067
and just enjoyed the show.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:29.834
It was a fantastic
"Bright Mississippi" show.

00:01:29.834 --> 00:01:34.033
And when the lights came up,
people looked over at the table.

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:37.901
There's Madonna talking
to my wife Diana and myself.

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:40.167
And then went --
"Nah, couldn't be."

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.667
-"There's no way
Elvis Costello..."

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:45.133
-And we had a lovely evening.

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:46.934
We had a lovely evening.
Great music, yeah.

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:48.067
-That's so fun.

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:49.701
That's wild.
I love the Village Vanguard.

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:51.133
I miss that.
-It is. It's --

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:53.400
All the places, we've just got
to give them lots of love.

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:54.767
And that's what we're saying,
you know?

00:01:54.767 --> 00:01:56.567
We're playing Pier 17
tomorrow night

00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:58.467
here in New York City.

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:00.300
[ Cheering ]

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.167
-You actually have
an announcement

00:02:03.167 --> 00:02:04.734
that you'd like to
announce tonight on the show.

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:06.901
-Yeah, oh. Can I tell them?
-Please tell them.

00:02:06.901 --> 00:02:12.434
-I'm gonna play a 10-night stand
in New York City next February,

00:02:12.434 --> 00:02:13.534
but here's the thing --

00:02:13.534 --> 00:02:16.767
[ Cheering ]

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:19.801
I'm gonna print a list
of 10 songs a night

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:22.234
that's gonna give you the clue

00:02:22.234 --> 00:02:24.367
to what that night's
gonna be like.

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:26.367
And the other 10 songs
that I might play

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:27.534
are a secret.

00:02:27.534 --> 00:02:29.767
So you'll never hear
the same song twice.

00:02:29.767 --> 00:02:32.667
It's gonna be 200 songs
over 10 nights.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.634
-So you can go every single
night if you want to?

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.400
-You can come. We'll give you
a special price.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.000
You want to come 10 nights?
You want to come 10 nights?

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.868
[ Cheering ]

00:02:39.868 --> 00:02:44.534
One price, you can get
a completely different price

00:02:44.534 --> 00:02:45.767
if you don't want to
come at all.

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:47.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.067
-If you don't want to
come at all,

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:50.367
I'll give you 20 bucks
to not come.

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:51.834
-Second price.

00:02:51.834 --> 00:02:53.667
-Where is it?
Where are you performing?

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:55.067
-It's at the Gramercy Theater.

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:57.167
It's a beautiful theater.
-Oh, I love that theater.

00:02:57.167 --> 00:03:01.033
-Played there a few years ago
with The Impostors,

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:03.167
The Impostors and Charlie Sexton
will be with me

00:03:03.167 --> 00:03:05.033
tomorrow night, but also,

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.934
we've got our mate, Nick Lowe.

00:03:06.934 --> 00:03:09.067
That's pretty great, you know?

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:11.167
Nick Lowe and The Straitjackets.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:12.868
We're on the road now.

00:03:12.868 --> 00:03:15.467
But -- But --

00:03:15.467 --> 00:03:18.200
you have a different
exclusive here.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.400
You see this here picture?

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.567
Can you see that at all?

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.300
-Yeah.
-See that?

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:28.300
That's me at 17,
on New Year's Day of 1972.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:30.567
My friend Allan Mayes is here,
my partner from Liverpool

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:32.634
who asked me to join his band.

00:03:32.634 --> 00:03:36.400
And, you know, we've been going
our different ways since then.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:38.267
We played for about
a year together.

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:40.133
And look at this.

00:03:40.133 --> 00:03:44.901
This is his school exercise book
he kept all these years.

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:47.367
It lists every show
we ever played.

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:48.868
-Can I see it?
-Yeah.

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:51.200
You can touch it.
You can put the white gloves on.

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:54.133
-This is real.
Look, "Rusty's Gigs."

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.200
This is your gigs.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:57.133
-Yeah, gigs from 1971.

00:03:57.133 --> 00:04:00.467
Optimistically,
there's no other date.

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:01.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:01.501 --> 00:04:03.133
-Wow.
-And we're here tonight!

00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:04.534
-2022!

00:04:04.534 --> 00:04:05.734
-Now, here,
I'll tell you the story.

00:04:05.734 --> 00:04:07.667
Allan rang me up and he said,
"You know,

00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:10.234
it would be 50 years since we
started our partnership."

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:12.701
We would play everywhere
in Liverpool

00:04:12.701 --> 00:04:14.200
where they would let us,

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.133
and a few places where
they wouldn't let us.

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:17.334
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:19.601
Like, we played the
Catholic girls' school,

00:04:19.601 --> 00:04:21.667
Mary Help of Christians,

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:24.801
known locally as
"Mary, Feed the Pigeons."

00:04:24.801 --> 00:04:26.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.234 --> 00:04:30.400
And we were paid only
in furtive glances

00:04:30.400 --> 00:04:32.601
and unfulfilled promises.

00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.701
[ Laughter ]
-That's the contract you got?

00:04:34.701 --> 00:04:38.033
-Actually, the ledger says
we were paid absolutely nil,

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:39.767
and that was between two of us.

00:04:39.767 --> 00:04:42.434
-Wow, yeah. You split nil.

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:46.234
-And actually, the gig that
I played 50 years ago tonight

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:48.067
is in here, and I was late.

00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:49.968
And I still got paid half.

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:53.534
-So this is all the gigs
and all the songs?

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:54.968
-All the songs, and so there's

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:56.567
all the songs we did
by other people.

00:04:56.567 --> 00:04:58.133
We wrote a few of our own tunes.

00:04:58.133 --> 00:05:01.067
"The Resurrection of Rust"
is a record --

00:05:01.067 --> 00:05:04.367
Allan rang me up and he said,
"Do you want to get together?

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:06.234
It's been 50 years since
we started playing together.

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:07.901
Do you want to make a cassette?"

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:09.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.434 --> 00:05:11.467
I said...

00:05:11.467 --> 00:05:13.400
"No.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.934
Let's make the record
we would have made

00:05:14.934 --> 00:05:16.467
if they'd let us
when we were 17."

00:05:16.467 --> 00:05:18.534
-Wow.
-So I got The Impostors

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:22.133
and my pals, and we went in
and we made this here record.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:24.701
Brand new. 50th anniversary.

00:05:24.701 --> 00:05:27.067
And we're gonna play a song by
Nick Lowe in a little while.

00:05:27.067 --> 00:05:31.167
-Yeah, I love "Everybody Knows
This is Nowhere."

00:05:31.167 --> 00:05:32.968
I love that.

00:05:32.968 --> 00:05:34.234
But I love "Maureen &amp; Sam."

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:35.534
It's one of my jams.
-Oh!

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.734
-And "Surrender to the Rhythm"
is my other big jam.

00:05:37.734 --> 00:05:38.734
-That's the one we're gonna
play tonight for you.

00:05:38.734 --> 00:05:39.868
-You're gonna play that tonight?

00:05:39.868 --> 00:05:40.834
-We're gonna play
"Surrender to the Rhythm."

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:42.133
-For me? That's amazing.

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:44.300
[ Applause ]
That's my jam, right there.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.334
-In honor of Madonna,
if nothing else.

00:05:46.334 --> 00:05:48.868
-In honor of Madonna,
Elvis Costello, everybody!

00:05:48.868 --> 00:05:51.901
"The Resurrection of Rust"
is out now.

00:05:51.901 --> 00:05:53.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:55.901
Elvis and Allan Mayes perform
after the break.

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:57.467
Stick around, everybody!

